-- A chained printout such as |?Has characteristic.Has length value costs
-- O(rows^2) entity cache lookups. On a memcached backed wiki that is one
-- network round trip each, so it dominates everything else: over 3000 rows a
-- single chained column issues 9,021,486 lookups and takes 28 minutes, where
-- the same property unchained issues 9,000 and takes 0.9s. Measured against
-- SMW 7.3.1 with the SPARQL store, whose printout fetching is the SQL store.
--
-- ItemFetcher::fetch() bypasses isCached() whenever isChain is set. That is
-- required for a later chain element, whose $dataItems are the previous
-- element's per subject output and therefore differ on every call. It is not
-- required for the first element, which is always handed $this->dataItems,
-- the complete and immutable result list of the QueryResult, so it re-runs
-- one identical prefetch per subject. Each run walks the whole list through
-- CacheWarmer::prepareCache and DisplayTitleFinder::prefetchFromList, which
-- is one cache lookup per list entry, hence the square.
--
-- PrefetchCache::prefetch() already memoises, but only after warming the
-- cache and fingerprinting the list, so the guard has to sit in front of it.
-- The memo is keyed on PrefetchCache's own value identity, so two printouts
-- of the same property with different request options cannot be conflated,
-- and it is held on the ItemFetcher instance, which is created per
-- QueryResult and owns the PrefetchCache it guards, so nothing survives the
-- query. The non first chain path is untouched.
--
-- After: the same column issues 21,056 lookups and takes 25s, and the cost
-- is linear in the row count rather than quadratic. Result sets verified
-- unchanged over 21 query shapes covering two and three hop chains, several
-- chained columns in one query, chains mixed with direct printouts, shared
-- and per row intermediates, rows with no value for the chained property,
-- inverse chains, and the same property printed three times with different
-- request options.
